# Decision Bug Hunter reads these variables from the process environment only.
# It never loads this or any other .env file. Export the variables in your
# shell for one session and unset them afterwards; see README.md.
#
# Required judge selection, unless --judge is passed: openai or microsoft.
# openai is OpenAI Decisions; microsoft is Microsoft-Decision-1 (experimental).
# There is no default and DBH never infers a judge from a route or a key; with
# neither set it exits 3 with NEED_USER_INPUT judge before any source read.
DBH_JUDGE=
#
# Required route selection, unless --provider is passed: openai, openrouter or
# foundry. The route must be one of the judge's: openai or openrouter for the
# openai judge; openrouter or foundry for the microsoft judge. DBH never picks
# a provider because a key happens to be set; with neither set it exits 3 with
# NEED_USER_INPUT provider before any source read.
DBH_PROVIDER=
#
# The selected route's key. Without it every scan exits 2 with
# provider_unavailable before any source read, output or network use.
# openai: api.openai.com, model gpt-6-luna.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# openrouter: openrouter.ai; one key serves both judges. Models:
# openai/gpt-6-luna-decisions (openai judge) and
# microsoft/microsoft-decision-1 (microsoft judge).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#
# foundry (microsoft judge only; not yet verified live): your own Microsoft
# Foundry resource. The endpoint is https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com and
# the deployment name is sent as the model. Both are required (or the
# --foundry-endpoint and --foundry-deployment flags).
DBH_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT=
DBH_FOUNDRY_DEPLOYMENT=
# Credential: set exactly one of the two, or set both and pass --foundry-auth
# api-key | entra-token to choose. AZURE_API_KEY is a resource key (sent as the
# api-key header); AZURE_ENTRA_TOKEN is a pre-acquired Microsoft Entra token
# (sent as a bearer token; DBH never acquires or refreshes one).
AZURE_API_KEY=
AZURE_ENTRA_TOKEN=
#
# Optional OpenAI routing identifiers, sent as the OpenAI-Organization and
# OpenAI-Project headers exactly as the official SDKs do (openai route only).
OPENAI_ORG_ID=
OPENAI_PROJECT_ID=
